  <section class="card" id="s01">
    <div class="section-grid">
      <div class="rail-number">01</div>
      <div class="section-body">
        <h2>Fall Campaign</h2>
        <p>This is a communication brief for the new Campminder homepage at campminder.com.</p>
        <p>The presentation concept is designed to mostly work inside the existing site. Same shell, same navigation, same interior pages.</p>
        <p>The page presentation isn’t final. We're open to your perspective and want to produce the best homepage possible, even if it looks and feels different from this concept.</p>

        <div class="label"><span class="lnum">01-01</span>Context</div>
        <p>The homepage has stayed static for a while. This fall, Campminder is shipping a host of new product features, including a new Registration flow, Campminder Intelligence, and the Ask Camp assistant inside Campanion.</p>

        <div class="label"><span class="lnum">01-02</span>Pressure</div>
        <div class="rows">
          <div class="row"><div class="row-num">01-02-A</div><div class="row-text"><strong>Momentum.</strong> Campfront is a newer competitor that publishes constantly and reads as software built for a younger generation of camp directors.</div></div>
          <div class="row"><div class="row-num">01-02-B</div><div class="row-text"><strong>Trust.</strong> Around 1,700 camps run on Campminder, most of them for years. That record is the strongest asset the page has and the hardest one for a newer platform to answer. We're only including content about live features that can be accessed today. We don't want to make any promises about future updates that haven't materialized.</div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="label"><span class="lnum">01-03</span>Audience</div>
        <p>Visitors to the Campminder website are typically camps shopping for a platform, and existing customers on their way to log in. The page works for both or it doesn’t work.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 02 -->
  <section class="card" id="s02">
    <div class="section-grid">
      <div class="rail-number">02</div>
      <div class="section-body">
        <h2>Territory</h2>

        <p>The territory is the conceptual foundation for every piece of communication in the campaign. It extends through the homepage, the sales conversation, the emails, and the social posts, so all of them tell one story.</p>
        <p>This territory says that Campminder is one comprehensive platform covering every role at a camp, with the people and the intelligence behind it.</p>

        <div class="copycard">
          <h3>One for all.</h3>
          <p class="cc-sub">One platform for everyone your camp connects to.</p>
          <p class="copy">Directors fill their camp. Staff get hired and show up ready. Parents register every kid in one pass. Registration, staffing, health, communication, and the business behind it all, with Campminder Intelligence running underneath and a camp success team that has your back.</p>
          <p class="cc-close">Take the tour, or we’ll walk you through it.</p>
          <p class="cc-tagrow"><span class="tagline">Unpack possible.</span><span class="pill filled">Book a demo</span></p>
        </div>

        <div class="label">Hierarchy</div>
        <p>The hierarchy is how different types of information combine across all of our communication channels.</p>

        <div class="hier">
          <div class="block leadblock">
            <div class="brole">Conceptual lead</div>
            <div class="nm">One for all</div>
            <div class="role">One platform, every role at camp.</div>
            <div class="bdiv"></div>
            <span class="use-l">Implemented</span>
            <ul class="use">
              <li>Homepage hero</li>
              <li>Conceptual foundation for email, social, sales</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="hier-side">
            <div class="block">
              <div class="brole">Narrative support</div>
              <div class="nm">An extension of your team</div>
              <div class="role">The people who run the platform with you.</div>
              <div class="bdiv"></div>
              <span class="use-l">Implemented</span>
              <ul class="use">
                <li>Homepage camp success section</li>
                <li>Overall copywriting tone</li>
                <li>Sales conversations</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="block">
              <div class="brole">Structural support</div>
              <div class="nm">Built by people who know camp</div>
              <div class="role">Features introduced by the person who does the work.</div>
              <div class="bdiv"></div>
              <span class="use-l">Implemented</span>
              <ul class="use">
                <li>Homepage role and feature blocks</li>
                <li>Social and email positioning</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

