  <!-- 04 -->
  <section class="card" id="s04">
    <div class="section-grid">
      <div class="rail-number">04</div>
      <div class="section-body">
        <h2>UX requests</h2>
        <p>Set in working sessions with Campminder.</p>

        <div class="rows">
          <div class="row"><div class="row-num">04-01</div><div class="row-text"><strong>A class of its own.</strong> Campfront has a corner on the AI/SaaS look that you see on every other technology site. There's room for an editorial, trustworthy page that quietly reads as quality and longevity rather than vibe-coded modernity.</div></div>
          <div class="row"><div class="row-num">04-02</div><div class="row-text"><strong>Show the product.</strong> Real screens, current at launch. Ideally, every claim has something visible sitting next to it. The concept leans on product screens, with photography primarily in the hero and the team block.</div></div>
          <div class="row"><div class="row-num">04-03</div><div class="row-text"><strong>Motion where a task completes.</strong> A form filling, a dashboard assembling. Anywhere where we can show work getting done on the Campminder platform.</div></div>
          <div class="row"><div class="row-num">04-03</div><div class="row-text"><strong>Real people, real camps.</strong> Customer camps and actual Campminder staff. Nothing clearly stock or fake. These customers know each other and spot anything staged.</div></div>
          <div class="row"><div class="row-num">04-04</div><div class="row-text"><strong>Plain language.</strong> No acronyms, nothing to decode. This audience is proud of being camp people rather than technology people.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 05 -->
  <section class="card" id="s05">
    <div class="section-grid">
      <div class="rail-number">05</div>
      <div class="section-body">
        <h2>Guardrails</h2>
        <p>Set in working sessions with Campminder.</p>

        <div class="rows">
          <div class="row"><div class="row-num">05-01</div><div class="row-text"><strong>No pain-point selling.</strong> We don’t remind directors that their job is hard. They know. We show what they get.</div></div>
          <div class="row"><div class="row-num">05-02</div><div class="row-text"><strong>No future tense.</strong> If it isn’t live, it isn’t on the page. No coming soon, no roadmap, no dates.</div></div>
          <div class="row"><div class="row-num">05-03</div><div class="row-text"><strong>No speed claims.</strong> Speed is shown by a visible release record, never asserted.</div></div>
          <div class="row"><div class="row-num">05-04</div><div class="row-text"><strong>No running against anyone.</strong> No competitor named, referenced, or answered. No comparison tables, no versus pages.</div></div>
          <div class="row"><div class="row-num">05-05</div><div class="row-text"><strong>No tech talk without a use.</strong> Modern under the hood, plain on the page. Technical language earns its place only when a camp director can act on it.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

